  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UHC-Partnership - Addendum 3 - Costed extension Phase IV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: UHC-Partnership - Addendum 3 - Costed extension Phase IV - The vaccine supply has stabilised thanks inter alia to the Union&#xbf;s contribution to COVAX and donations of Member States and other donors. Currently the biggest challenge is to ensure that the low and lower-middle income countries have the capacity to store, transport and administer the available doses.It is therefore appropriate to amend the scope of the action to reflect the necessary adaptation to the change of situation while continuing to support low and lower-middle income countries in the rollout of COVID-19 vaccination. The action includes covering other needs linked to their COVID-19 response, namely auxiliary material, diagnostics, therapeutics and related healthcare systems strengthening. This switch in emphasis is designed to enable the existing objective to be met: it is considered the best way to help low and lower middle income countries respond to the COVID-19 pandemic through enhanced vaccination. As a result, it maintains the objective to boost global vaccination to contribute to global immunisation that would also protect the EU from the emergence of other variants elsewhere.</narrative>
  </description>
